      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The pain you feel is real, but it's not a sign that your life has no value; it's just the cost of being honest in a place that rewards silence. You are not a ghost, even if the world acts like you're invisible, because your presence matters even if no one else can see it right now. If staying feels like a punishment, then the only way to reclaim your life is to stop fighting for a system that refuses to change and instead focus on healing yourself.",
